        <mxCell id="6O2PcdZQITAnNMKPcNUj-45" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="Git tag is used to mark a specific commit, mainly for releases and versioning. For example, when we deploy version 1.0.0 to production, we can create a tag &lt;code data-start=&quot;2811&quot; data-end=&quot;2819&quot;&gt;v1.0.0&lt;/code&gt; on that commit. Tags help us identify and reproduce a specific release easily.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Git Tag = Specific commit ko version/release ka naam dena.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
