        <mxCell id="o667PHzVvcjDVYQr-MMa-46" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" value="OIDC authentication ka mechanism hai jo GitHub Actions jaise external platform ko Azure App/Service Principal ke saath securely authenticate karata hai." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="560" x="-1400" y="28460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="o667PHzVvcjDVYQr-MMa-47" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" value="&lt;table&gt;&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Managed Identity&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Service Principal&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;OIDC&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Kya hai?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Azure-managed identity&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Application identity&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Authentication mechanism&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Secret required?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;❌ No&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Traditionally ✅, but OIDC ke saath ❌&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;❌ No long-lived secret&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Identity kaun manage karta?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Azure&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;You/Entra&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GitHub + Entra trust&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Typical use&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Azure → Azure&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;App/Terraform/automation&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GitHub Actions → Azure&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Example&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;VM → Key Vault&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Terraform → Azure&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GitHub Actions → Azure&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="560" x="-1400" y="28520" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="o667PHzVvcjDVYQr-MMa-48" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" value="&lt;p data-start=&quot;3165&quot; data-end=&quot;3209&quot; class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;3165&quot; data-end=&quot;3209&quot;&gt;&quot;Managed Identity vs Service Principal?&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchor&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;3211&quot; data-end=&quot;3215&quot;&gt;Bol:&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;blockquote data-start=&quot;3217&quot; data-end=&quot;3542&quot;&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;3219&quot; data-end=&quot;3542&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;3219&quot; data-end=&quot;3542&quot;&gt;Managed Identity is an Azure-managed identity assigned to Azure resources, which allows them to access other Azure services without managing credentials. A Service Principal is an application identity in Microsoft Entra ID that can be used by applications, automation tools, or CI/CD pipelines to authenticate to Azure.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;3544&quot; data-end=&quot;3566&quot;&gt;Phir agar OIDC pooche:&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;blockquote data-start=&quot;3568&quot; data-end=&quot;3834&quot;&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;3570&quot; data-end=&quot;3834&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;3570&quot; data-end=&quot;3834&quot;&gt;OIDC allows an external workload such as GitHub Actions to authenticate to Azure without storing a long-lived client secret. GitHub issues an OIDC token, and Microsoft Entra ID validates the token through a federated credential associated with the application.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="450" width="560" x="-1400" y="28770" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="o667PHzVvcjDVYQr-MMa-51" edge="1" parent="1" source="o667PHzVvcjDVYQr-MMa-49" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;" target="o667PHzVvcjDVYQr-MMa-50" value="">
