        <mxCell id="RYsPmi5vES3W1vmxjtKf-43" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="parallel Jobs" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="120" x="50" y="22327.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RYsPmi5vES3W1vmxjtKf-46" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;rounded=0;" value="Agar interviewer pooche:&quot;What are the requirements to run pipelines in parallel in Azure DevOps?&quot;Tum bolo:&quot;First, we need sufficient parallel job capacity in the Azure DevOps organization. Second, we need sufficient agents in the agent pool, especially when using self-hosted agents. Each agent should have the required tools and capabilities. For example, if I want to run three jobs simultaneously, I need three available parallel job slots and suitable agents to execute those jobs.&quot;&lt;div&gt;🧠 Bas ye formula yaad rakh:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Parallel Pipeline = Parallel Job Capacity + Available Agents + Required Agent Capabilities&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Aur ek correction jo interview me kaam aayegi: Microsoft-hosted agents me tum normally individual agent machines manage nahi karte; Azure DevOps dynamically agents provide karta hai. Self-hosted setup me tumhe agents maintain/manage karne padte hain.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="155" width="540" x="240" y="22265" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RYsPmi5vES3W1vmxjtKf-48" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="dev- agent pool --&amp;gt;agent&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;test&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;prod&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="470" x="240" y="22430" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RYsPmi5vES3W1vmxjtKf-49" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&quot;What is a multi-stage pipeline in Azure DevOps?&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchor&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tum bolo:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&quot;A multi-stage pipeline is a single Azure DevOps pipeline that contains multiple stages for different purposes, such as build, testing and deployment to Dev, UAT and Production. We can also configure dependencies, conditions and approvals between stages. For example, after successful testing, the Dev stage runs, then UAT, and after approval the Production deployment runs.&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&quot;One pipeline → Multiple stages → Build → Test → Dev → UAT → Prod.&quot;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="280" width="520" x="210" y="22500" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RYsPmi5vES3W1vmxjtKf-50" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="364.07" width="520" x="210" y="22780" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RYsPmi5vES3W1vmxjtKf-51" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="maan lo meri ek pipeline jo ki 30 min le rahi h but idelly&amp;nbsp; 5-10 min lagna chiye then how to optimizate the pipeline?" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="500" x="220" y="23160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RYsPmi5vES3W1vmxjtKf-52" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" value="if the pipeline is slow , first i will identify in which satges is taking the more time for the excution of pipeline using the pipeline logs. then i will optimize the specific stage.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;to optimizate the pipeline&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. enable the cache for dependences (terraform init - provider hota h tho jinti pipeline sabhi m dowload hoga provider ---&amp;gt; providers/plugin cache enable--&amp;gt;pipeline baar baar provider ko download nhi krege aur ye mera cache h uda kr use kr lega )&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Reduce the unnecessary task&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. we can use the parallel jobs to reduce the time&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4.use a properly size build agents&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;5. monitoring pipeline performance regularly&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="460" x="240" y="23200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RYsPmi5vES3W1vmxjtKf-53" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="366.73" width="460" x="240" y="23390" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
