        <mxCell id="VfkdXgMbOGRIXH-vw9D5-18" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=0;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" value="ARM (azure resource manager)&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot;&gt;Haan bhai, &lt;strong&gt;ARM (Azure Resource Manager)&lt;/strong&gt; ko Azure DevOps ke context mein simple language mein samjho:&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchor&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ARM kya hai?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ARM Azure ka management layer/API hai&lt;/strong&gt;, jiske through Azure resources ko &lt;strong&gt;create, update, delete, configure aur access-control&lt;/strong&gt; kiya jata hai.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Azure DevOps khud directly VM, VNet, Storage, Key Vault etc. ko manage nahi karta. Pipeline Azure se interact karne ke liye &lt;strong&gt;Azure Resource Manager / Azure APIs&lt;/strong&gt; ko use karti hai.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
